# Dedicated manifest: A46b needs a 16-frame / 2-anchor ladder at T_lat=4 per
# anchor, which NO other arm uses — its cache is a new extraction, not the
# 20-frame a24h cache that S2E and A46 read. Reusing that cache would silently
# return wrong tensors: keys are {dataset}_{site}_{origin} and do not encode
# the ladder. It also runs a 239-token sequence (196 visual), so it needs a
# smaller per-device batch than the sweep default. Launch only with:
#   MANIFEST=configs/ablation/A46b.manifest N_VIS=2 \
#   VJEPA_CACHE_VER=vit_large_f16_s224_nonhrv_sp45_a24h \
#   BATCH_SIZE=8 ACCUM=2 NPACKS=1 bash scripts/ablation_sweep.sh
#
# Extract the cache first (~420 G, ~16 h GPU) and free the 210 G s2d cache to
# stay under the 1 TB quota. Do NOT free the 525 G a24h cache — S2E and A46
# are this arm's comparands.
#
# ID   | MODE  | STAGE | MODEL_CFG             | SEEDS    | BASE
A46b  | train | s2e   | vision_chronos2_s2e   | 42,43,44 | uk_pv_s1_selfattn_s{seed}
